  "body": "Third slice of #1250: a reference page for the turning operations, `site/content/guide/operations-turning.md`, linked from `guide/operations.md`.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 37482923fc858b4ba3c4c600504020ef2489f1b0).\n\n## What changed\n- New page with a shared section (no picks / Boundary does not apply, tool kind per operation, the spindle-axis law, constant surface speed and feed per rev, the workholding rpm ceiling, holder checks, the work-spindle rule for milling kinds and live tooling), then one section per turning kind: what it is for and when to choose it over a neighbour, its tabs with units and seed defaults, and the refusals a user is most likely to meet (message stems quoted from source).\n- One link line in `guide/operations.md`, at the end of \"The settings tabs\" - away from the lines #1260 and #1264 add.\n\n## Kinds and sources\nThe twelve `Section::Turning` rows of `KindInfo::ALL` (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`): Facing, Profile Rough, Profile Finish, Groove Rough, Groove Finish, Parting (Part), Threading, Chamfering (Chamfer), Taper Turning (Taper), Multi-Pass Turning (Multi-Pass), Form Turning (Form), Boring (Bore).\n- Defaults: the `seed_*` fns in `kinds.rs` over `operation/seed.rs` (feed 1200, plunge 300, clearance 25 above stock top, model top/bottom).\n- Tabs and labels: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/turning_page.rs`, `turning_more_page.rs`, `op_tabs.rs` (Machine tab = \"Bar feeder\" for Part only).\n- Tool kinds: `operation/tool_law.rs`, `tool_gate.rs`; tool fields: `egui_app/pages.rs`, `tool_turning_row.rs`.\n- Lathe concepts: `cutting_turn.rs` (G96 kinds, Threading G97), `setup_workholding.rs`, `operation/spindle_law.rs`, `operation/turning_holder.rs`, `lathe_voice.rs`, `operation/types/area.rs`.\n- Refusals: `crates/motion/src/turning/{face,prof,blade,parting,thread,form}.rs`, `contour/rides.rs`, `bore/doors.rs`, `bore/mod.rs`.\n\n## Weight and overlap\n`weight = 5`, the same scheme #1260 (`operations-2d.md`) and #1264 (`operations-3d.md`) use. `git merge-tree --write-tree` of this branch against `origin/issue/1250-docs-op-reference` and `origin/issue/1250-docs-op-reference-3d` is clean each way (and 2D+3D merge clean with each other).\n\n## How tested\nDocs only. `zola` is not installed on this machine, so `zola check` was not run; the internal links (`@/guide/operations.md`, `@/guide/refusals.md`, `@/guide/operations-turning.md`) point at files on main.\n\n## Not exercised / left out\n- No toolpath pictures (as in the first two slices).\n- Remaining families for #1250: multi-axis, probing, plasma, wire/sinker EDM (once shipped), plus a toolpath picture per kind.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (docs slice, no escalation)\n\nRefs #1250\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
